  "id": "Compound::DB00304 - Gene::2099",
  "verbalization": "Desogestrel, a progestin, is implicated in the regulation of estrogen receptor alpha (Esr1) through its inclusion in the Progesterone Congeners class, which includes Norgestimate, Ethynodiol, and Etonogestrel. All three compounds bind to Esr1, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the activation or modulation of the estrogen receptor. The shared ancestry of these compounds within the Progesterone Congeners class indicates a potential for similar molecular interactions, reinforcing the hypothesis that Desogestrel may exert its effects through a shared pathway involving Esr1. The low scores in the final_score metric suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but the consistent binding to Esr1 across different progestins supports a mechanistic link. The presence of a common lowest common ancestor (LCA) in the Steroid and Progestin classes further underscores the biological relevance of this interaction. While the evidence is robust, the exact mechanism by which Desogestrel influences Esr1 remains to be fully elucidated, necessitating further experimental validation.",
